# Your Brand Looks Different Everywhere Customers Find You

Your website, social profiles, and directory listings all describe your business differently.

When your business name, description, and details vary across your website, social profiles, and directory listings, it splits your entity signal for search engines and AI systems, and it looks inconsistent to a prospect doing due diligence across multiple sources.

Symptoms:
- Different business descriptions on your site versus your social profiles
- Inconsistent business name, address, or contact details across listings
- Directory profiles that were set up once and never updated
- No single, approved brand description used consistently

Our solution: We audit every public-facing profile and listing, standardize your business name, description, and details into one consistent, approved version, and update it everywhere, giving search engines and AI systems a clear, consistent entity to recognize.

FAQs:

Q: Does this affect SEO rankings directly?
A: It primarily strengthens entity recognition and trust signals, which support both traditional search visibility and AI citation likelihood.

Q: How often should this be reviewed?
A: An annual review is a reasonable baseline, with updates any time your business details genuinely change.